.SH NAME
ktm-json \- Parsing, querying, encoding and decoding JSON, structs included.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import json;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Parsing, querying, encoding and decoding JSON, structs included.
.SH TYPES
.SS State
.EX
struct State {
        u8 ch;
        i64 offset;
        i64 error;
        i64 line;
        i64 col;
};
.EE
.SS Value
.EX
struct Value {
        State *state;
        Value *next;
        i64 type;
        u8[] key;
        union
        {
                Value *array;
                Value *object;
                u8[] str;
                u8 *strnum;
                f64 floatVal;
                i64 intVal;
                bool boolean;
        };
};
.EE
.SS Reader
.EX
struct Reader
{
    u8[] text;
    i64 pos;
    i64 depth;
    i64 cap;
    ReaderLevel *levels;
    u8[] k;
    String buf;
    bool strict;
};
.EE
.PP
Reads JSON text front to back without building a tree: open an object with beginObject() and loop on nextKey(), open an array with beginArray() and loop on nextItem(), and read each value with readString/readInt/readFloat/readBool (isNull() first where null is allowed, skipValue() for one you don't want). A wrong value throws ERR_DECODE with where it is: "3:14: lines[2].price: expected a number, got a string". Make one with json.readerNew(text) (the text is viewed, not copied: keep it alive) and free it with r.free(). Its fields are read-only outside module json.
.SS Writer
.EX
struct Writer
{
    String out;
    i64 indent;
    i64 depth;
    bool done;
    u8 levels[MAX_DEPTH];
};
.EE
.PP
Builds a JSON document into a String: begin/end the arrays and objects, key() each member, and add the values; commas, quotes and escapes are written for you. Make one with json.writerNew() (a declared Writer is all zero, not set up), free it with w.free(), and take the text with w.take(). Its fields are read-only outside module json.
